# AGENTS.md


- What the project is, and the domain glossary: `CONTEXT.md`. Take terms only from there.
- Decisions and why: `docs/adr/` (format: `docs/adr/README.md`).
- Code rules for review: `CODING_STANDARDS.md`.
- A package belongs to the family by its distribution name `rb-*`, not by its command: the command may differ from the slug — never rename one to match the other (Standard, Technology).
- The package Standard: https://github.com/bolandeu/python-package-gate/blob/main/skills/cli-builder/reference/standard.md (sections by name, for example «Install»).
- Portability: `pathlib` and `platformdirs` for paths, explicit UTF-8 for text, UTC and `time.monotonic` for time, atomic writes through `os.replace`, OS-specific behaviour behind one small interface, no `shell=True`, no `os.fork`.
- Addresses are deployment, not code: no package-index URL, registry host or credential name in `pyproject.toml`, in the package or in the wheel metadata. An index, if the deployment has one, is `UV_INDEX`; the release channel is the asset of a `vX.Y.Z` tag.
- The gate before a commit: `gate check`, on this machine — the command is `uvx --from "git+https://github.com/bolandeu/python-package-gate.git@<template tag>#subdirectory=gate" gate check` (Standard, CI). It is the only gate: no workflow runs it.

